        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "7dcc6f77-9f5b-57b0-80fb-f1c15499912f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Maryland Jockey Club\n- Places: Baltimore, Laurel, Bowie, Prince George's County, Maryland\n- Facilities: Pimlico Race Course, Laurel Park Racecourse, Bowie Race Track\n- Topics: Bowie city growth and rankings\n\nFacts:\n- Maryland Jockey Club has remained the corporate name of the company that operates horse racing venues for 267 years.\n- Pimlico Race Course in Baltimore, Maryland, opened in 1870.\n- Laurel Park Racecourse in Laurel, Maryland, opened in 1911.\n- Bowie Race Track in Bowie, Maryland, opened as a race course in 1914.\n- Bowie Race Track in Bowie, Maryland, ceased operations as a track in 1985.\n- Bowie grew from a small railroad stop into the largest municipality in Prince George's County, Maryland.\n- Bowie is the fifth most populous city in Maryland.\n- Bowie is the third largest city by area in Maryland.",
